  "body": "# Associated User Story\n<br>\nAs an officer, I want to import event data from GetInvolved into our website, so I don't have to recreate events for the next semester.\n\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n<br>\n\n\n**Officers upload the Excel/CSV export they download from GetInvolved. They see a preview showing how each row maps to an event before confirming. Once confirmed, the events are added to our website with correct details.**\n\n- Sunny:  An officer opens the events list, clicks \"Import from GetInvolved,\" and uploads the Excel/CSV file exported from GetInvolved. They see a preview of the events to be imported (event name, date, time, location, point type, description) with per-row mapping and any issues flagged. They confirm, and the events are added to our website with correct details. They see a summary (e.g., \"12 events imported, 2 skipped\"). Importing a row that already corresponds to an existing event updates it rather than creating a duplicate. No private member information is ever imported.\n\n- Rainy: The upload fails, the file is the wrong format, columns are missing or mismatched, an event is missing required details (date, location, etc.), the file is empty, or a regular member tries to import. The system shows a clear error (e.g., \"Please upload an .xlsx or .csv file\" or \"Row 5 is missing an event date\") instead of failing silently or importing partial events. Problem rows are listed so the officer can fix them. Valid rows can still be imported while problem rows are held back. Nothing is saved until the officer confirms. Only officers can use the import tool.\n\nDefinition of Done -\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied:\n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented;\n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes);\n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.",
